From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:01:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0062: the submission follows the GPU
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Kyty submitted one command buffer per command list of the game, 27 an image
in Astro Bot: 69 % of those submissions found the GPU drained, and the GPU
waited about 2 ms at every boundary for the kernel to hand it the next
buffer, 30 % of its time.

The scheduler now counts the draws and dispatches it records. Every 64, when
the GPU has at most one buffer in flight and nothing behind it, the buffer is
submitted, so the GPU finds the next job in its queue when it ends the
current one. At the end of a list the buffer is submitted unless the GPU has
two buffers of lookahead and this one is not full (4 096 commands). Before
the GPU thread sleeps, everything recorded goes: the game never waits for a
label of a buffer that was never submitted. The fixed points (suspension,
flip, waits) submit as before.

Measured on Astro Bot in the Celestial Garden: 5.53 → 6.55 images/s, the GPU
busy 72 → 82 %.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
